WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.801
-Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
This is it.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.067
Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.801
I read that Jeff Bezos
may partner with Jay-Z

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:13.334
to buy the NFL's
Washington Commanders.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.467
Bezos might be the only person
who has to stop and be like,

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.033
"Wait, do I already own
a football team?"

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.934
I'm rooting for Bezos and Jay-Z.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.267
I never thought I'd say this,
but after the last few weeks,

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.868
I just want some
normal billionaires.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:29.367
Don't you --
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.067
Can't they just be normal?

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.934
One of the big stories
today that I was reading

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.033
in the headlines that was funny,

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.434
Starbucks just rolled out their

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.934
holiday menu and their
25th anniversary holiday cups.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.234
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.234
Everywhere.
It's everywhere, yeah.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.467
We're so starved for good news,

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:47.901
we're now celebrating
the anniversary of a cup.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.734
We're like, "25 years of a cup!
Oh, my God!"

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:57.400
Tariq, you see this cup?
Let me text you this cup news.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.901
That's right --
Starbucks just rolled out

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:00.601
their holiday menu and cups.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:01.901
They even released
a special message.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:02.968
Check this out.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.567
-The holidays are here,

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.234
and Starbucks
is excited to bring back

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.367
all your holiday favorites,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.133
like holiday cups,

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.400
peppermint mochas,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.200
Michael Bublé CDs,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.567
holiday cups,

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.834
peppermint mochas,

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.634
Michael Bublé CDs,

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.000
[ Distorted ] holiday cups,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.267
peppermint mochas,

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.067
Michael Bublé CDs,

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.434
Oh, my God.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.067
It's only November.
What are we doing?

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.868
No, don't question it.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:33.467
Remember, must use Christmas
to sell coffee.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.033
So, happy holidays
from Starbucks.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.734
-Oh, yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:40.100
Yeah! I love that.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.534
Well, get this.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:46.033
Today, Netflix launched
their new ad-supported plan

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.467
for only $7 a month.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.367
[ Audience boos]

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.667
But this is interesting, though.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.434
Apparently, some Netflix shows
have exclusive sponsors.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.634
Did you hear about this?
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:56.734
First up, "Grace and Frankie"

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:59.934
is exclusively sponsored
by Activia.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.100
-Oh.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.701
-You know,
it's exclusive to the show.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.067
-Yeah.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:08.100
-"Squid Game" is sponsored by
Black Friday at Best Buy.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.067
I'm starting to understand it.
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.467
-Yeah, next,
"The Watcher" is sponsored by

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.067
this photo of
Senator Mark Kelly.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.467
You go, "Oh, wow.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.300
Okay, buddy. Okay."

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.667
Next up, "Stranger Things"
is sponsored by...

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.801
October Kanye.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.601
"Stranger Things."
-Wow!

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.133
-Next up, "Dahmer"
is sponsored by...

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.367
Impossible Meat.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:30.434
-Oh!

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.634
-What?
-Wow!

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:34.834
-And, finally, "Bridgerton"

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:38.434
is sponsored by
Brookstone "Back Massagers."

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.834
For your back.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.067
Switching gears.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.133
Last night at a train station
in Washington, D.C.,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.200
President Biden delivered
a speech about

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.767
protecting democracy.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:53.367
Yeah, normally, when a guy on a
train platform is yelling about

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:55.834
the country being doomed,
you just avoid eye contact

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.100
and keep moving.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:02:59.834
Some more political news.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.267
I heard that Florida governor
Ron DeSantis

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:04.868
is reconsidering
a presidential run in 2024

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.901
because he doesn't want to fight
former president Trump

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:07.968
for the nomination.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.501
That's a bummer.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:13.934
We were so close to a showdown
of Ronald versus Donald.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.534
Speaking of elections,
the midterms are this Tuesday,

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.701
and there are several
key races around the country.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.100
And while these races
can get heated,

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.834
it's important to remember
what the candidates

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.300
actually agree on.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.300
Here, let me show you
what I mean.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.767
First up,
John Fetterman and Dr. Oz

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:30.400
are facing off in Pennsylvania,
but they both can agree that...

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.400
Certain things you've got to be
able to agree on.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.634
-Yeah.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.067
-Next up, Blake Masters
is facing off against

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.801
Mark Kelly in Arizona.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.100
They can both agree that...

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.567
Up next, in Nevada, Susie Lee is
facing off against April Becker.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:50.968
They can both agree that...

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:59.567
"I'd just like to speak -- I'd
just like to speak to a manager.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:00.834
Here's another one.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.267
Angie Craig is facing off
against Tyler Kistner

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.968
in Minnesota,
but they can both agree that...

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.801
"Angie, there's no way

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:14.167
you're going to get this done
in three days."

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:22.267
Up next, Rudy Salas
is facing David Valadao.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.767
They're facing off
in California.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.000
They can both agree that...

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:33.901
-What?

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.167
-Next up, in Pennsylvania,

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:38.300
Matt Cartwright is
facing off against Jim Bognet.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.501
They can both agree...

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.467
What?
-That's odd.

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:48.300
-And, finally, Raphael Warnock
and Herschel Walker

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.734
are facing off in Georgia.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:50.968
They can both agree...

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:55.634
It's all bizarre.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:05:00.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.701
Well, some entertainment news.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:05.000
Yesterday, the new trailer for
"Avatar 2: The Way of Water"

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.067
was released.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.400
And as you guys have
probably heard,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.267
they shot the third movie,
as well, at the same time.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:12.334
so, today, they released
a trailer for "Avatar 3."

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:13.801
Yeah, take a look at this thing.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:16.734
-The way of water
connects all things.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:19.767
The unforgettable characters
of Pandora return,

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.234
like Jake and Neytiri,

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:24.734
along with majestic new
underwater heroes, such as...

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:29.100
And introducing...

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:40.200
-That looks good.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.534
Did you guys see this?

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:43.601
Elon Musk announced that
he's working with

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:47.200
Twitter engineers
on a reboot of Vine.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.033
Yeah, that could be ready
by the end of the year.

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.801
When Viners heard
Vine might make a comeback,

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:51.834
they were like...

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.267
-Yeah, I sure hope it does.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.234
-Meanwhile, kids who
only grew up with TikTok

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.033
are hearing about Vines
and thinking...

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.734
-What are those?!

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:11.634
-I mean, most people haven't
thought about Vine in a while,

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.901
so they were really surprised by
the news, kind of like...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.200
[ Horn honks ]

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:25.367
Some people think Elon Musk
is making too many changes

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:26.567
over at Twitter
and getting carried away,

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:27.601
kind of like...

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.734
But most people are excited
for Vine to return,

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:38.133
so here's hoping Elon
doesn't mess everything up,

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.033
kind of like...

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.801
-[ Sneezes ]

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:47.033
-"Nice, Ron."

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:51.534
Well, listen to this.

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.601
Next month, a model for E.T.
used in the movie

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:58.234
is expected to sell at auction
for $3 million.

00:06:58.234 --> 00:06:59.334
That's kind of cool,
but I don't know

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:00.968
who's going to buy that though,
you know?

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:03.734
I'm going to buy him!

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:09.400
Excuse me, sir?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.634
I said, I'm gonna buy me an E.T.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.901
I've been waiting
my whole life for this moment.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.300
I can use that dang E.T.
for all sorts of things.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.767
[ Laughs ]

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:21.434
Like what?

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:25.968
Well, I figure I can rest my
coffee mug on his head.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:28.267
I can put a wig on him,
take a picture,

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:30.934
and make it my profile picture
on my MySpace.

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:32.667
[ Laughs ]

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:35.400
I don't think people use
MySpace anymore.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.434
Yeah, I got all sorts of plans
for uses for an E.T.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.167
I can put him next to the dishes

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:42.667
and make it look like
he's warshing the dishes.

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:43.801
[ Laughs ]

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.133
Oh! I can take him to
a baseball game,

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.033
tell the stadium
it's his birthday,

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.767
then get him on the jumbotron
and have it say,

00:07:49.767 --> 00:07:51.367
"Happy birthday, E.T." on it."

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.501
And then, while everyone
is distracted wishing E.T.

00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:56.234
a happy birthday,
I can steal a bunch of hot dogs

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:57.501
from the concession stand.

00:07:57.501 --> 00:07:58.934
Then I got my dinner for
a whole year.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.133
[ Laughs ]

00:08:03.968 --> 00:08:05.300
Sounds like a plan,

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.767
but where are you going to get
$3 million to pay for it?

00:08:07.767 --> 00:08:09.701
Well, don't worry about it.

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:12.133
Just check me out on OnlyFans.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:15.400
[ Laughs ]

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:22.868
Finally, I saw that today is
National Sandwich Day.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.100
-Yeah!
-That's today.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.801
National Sandwich Day.

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:28.968
Hot-dog vendors were like,
"Do we celebrate this or..."

